WEBVTT

00:00:05.155 --> 00:00:07.656
Oxford bookworms, stage one.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:16.932
The president's murderer by Jennifer Bassett, read by Nicolette Mackenzie.

00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:21.924
The first day.

00:00:21.984 --> 00:00:23.926
Run.

00:00:23.986 --> 00:00:26.098
The man thought.

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.550
Move.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.214
Faster!

00:00:29.274 --> 00:00:32.736
I can't stop now!

00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:52.215
Over the man's head, the night sky was black and cold, and in front of him were the trees, tall, dark trees, 500 metres away.

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:58.588
I can hide there, the man thought.

00:00:58.648 --> 00:01:03.290
I can hide in those trees.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:09.402
They can't see me in the trees.

00:01:09.462 --> 00:01:13.084
He looked behind him.

00:01:13.144 --> 00:01:16.140
He could see the lights.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.308
There were five or six men.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:28.210
They ran fast, and their lights moved up and down.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.032
They were not far away now.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:37.575
He could hear their feet on the ground.

00:01:37.635 --> 00:01:41.798
The man ran faster.

00:01:41.858 --> 00:01:44.688
His legs were tired.

00:01:44.748 --> 00:01:48.230
His body was tired.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.740
There were noises in his head.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.011
He could not see.

00:01:55.071 --> 00:02:01.773
The trees were 200 meters away.

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:06.810
He wanted to stop running.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:15.061
He wanted to lie down and sleep.

00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:19.554
Then he heard a new noise.

00:02:19.614 --> 00:02:22.046
Dogs.

00:02:22.106 --> 00:02:26.808
They've got dogs, he thought.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:31.251
Oh no, not dogs.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:36.276
I can't run faster.

00:02:36.336 --> 00:02:38.929
But he did.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:41.060
Faster.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.812
And faster.

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:49.624
The trees were a hundred meters away.

00:02:49.684 --> 00:02:51.516
Fifty.

00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:53.886
Twenty.

00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:58.460
And then he was there.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:04.162
The trees opened their dark arms to him.

00:03:04.222 --> 00:03:08.253
but he did not stop running.

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:13.674
It was dark and quiet under the trees.

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:20.866
He ran first to the left and then to the right.

00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:33.102
He came to a hill, and for a second or two he stopped and listened.

00:03:33.162 --> 00:03:39.758
Then he heard the dogs again.

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:44.670
But he could not see the lights.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:49.733
Don't stop now, he thought.

00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:54.654
Dogs don't need eyes.

00:03:54.714 --> 00:04:00.268
They can find you in the dark.

00:04:00.328 --> 00:04:05.874
Quickly, he ran down the hill.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:13.909
It was very dark here, and he could not see very well.

00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:20.621
He ran into a tree, and nearly broke his arm.

00:04:20.681 --> 00:04:24.152
Careful, he thought.

00:04:24.212 --> 00:04:26.603
Careful!

00:04:26.663 --> 00:04:34.146
He put his hands out in front of him, and ran more slowly.

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:39.488
Then he heard a new noise.

00:04:39.547 --> 00:04:41.968
Water.

00:04:42.028 --> 00:04:45.400
A river, he thought.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:50.162
The dogs can't follow me across water.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:52.124
Where is it?

00:04:52.184 --> 00:04:54.095
Quick!

00:04:54.154 --> 00:04:59.216
Soon he found the river.

00:04:59.276 --> 00:05:06.068
It was not very big, but it ran quickly.

00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:12.380
The water was cold on his tired legs.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:24.094
He walked and ran up the river through the water for about two kilometers.

00:05:24.154 --> 00:05:30.617
Then he stopped and listened again.

00:05:30.676 --> 00:05:34.698
He could hear nothing.

00:05:34.758 --> 00:05:39.318
He stood there and waited.

00:05:39.378 --> 00:05:47.482
The trees watched him with dark, secret eyes.

00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:49.724
Nothing.

00:05:49.784 --> 00:05:51.915
No dogs.

00:05:51.974 --> 00:05:54.065
No lights.

00:05:54.125 --> 00:05:57.216
No noises.

00:05:57.275 --> 00:06:05.991
The man was cold now and very, very tired.

00:06:06.051 --> 00:06:10.785
I need sleep, he thought.

00:06:10.844 --> 00:06:15.278
Where can I hide?

00:06:15.338 --> 00:06:19.592
He looked up at the trees.

00:06:19.652 --> 00:06:23.525
Up there, he thought.

00:06:23.585 --> 00:06:27.882
The dogs can't follow me.

00:06:27.942 --> 00:06:30.288
up a tree.

00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:37.212
He found a tall tree and went up it.

00:06:37.272 --> 00:06:42.394
He could not see the ground now.

00:06:42.454 --> 00:06:50.788
He half sat, half stood in the tree and listened.

00:06:50.848 --> 00:06:55.577
Nothing.

00:06:55.637 --> 00:07:18.139
sleep for an hour, then go on, go south, hide in the day and move at night.

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:39.392
I can get there in five days, perhaps six The man put his head down on his arms and slept.

00:07:39.452 --> 00:07:43.715
What are you saying?

00:07:43.774 --> 00:07:45.295
You lost him?

00:07:45.315 --> 00:07:50.379
The chief of police said angrily.

00:07:50.438 --> 00:07:59.328
The young police inspector in front of her was tired, very tired.

00:07:59.388 --> 00:08:02.346
He wanted to sit down.

00:08:02.405 --> 00:08:07.570
But people did not sit down in the chief's office.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:11.062
They stood and waited.

00:08:11.122 --> 00:08:16.487
And perhaps the chief said, sit down.

00:08:16.546 --> 00:08:20.460
Then they sat down.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.732
But not before.

00:08:23.792 --> 00:08:28.037
So the inspector stood.

00:08:28.096 --> 00:08:32.389
I'm sorry chief," he said.

00:08:32.449 --> 00:08:37.030
We couldn't find him in the trees.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:39.902
We looked all night.

00:08:39.962 --> 00:08:50.534
But it was dark, and the chief of police put her hands on the desk in front of her.

00:08:50.594 --> 00:08:58.681
You had five men with you, Inspector, and two dogs.

00:08:58.741 --> 00:09:01.919
And you couldn't find him?

00:09:01.939 --> 00:09:13.300
Eva Hein, the chief of police, was a tall woman of about 50.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:19.488
Her eyes were grey and very cold.

00:09:19.548 --> 00:09:22.830
Dangerous eyes.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:27.103
When Eva Heim said, jump!

00:09:27.164 --> 00:09:29.356
People jumped.

00:09:29.416 --> 00:09:34.399
They did not ask questions first.

00:09:34.459 --> 00:09:43.547
The inspector waited, and the chief of police looked at him coldly.

00:09:43.607 --> 00:09:47.130
What are you waiting for?"

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.051
she asked.

00:09:49.111 --> 00:09:53.383
Go out and find him.

00:09:53.443 --> 00:10:05.068
Three months ago, this man, Alex Deenon, killed the president of our country.

00:10:05.128 --> 00:10:10.440
He's a murderer, a dangerous man.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:21.153
Twenty-four hours ago, He escaped from prison, and our new president wants him back in prison.

00:10:21.173 --> 00:10:27.275
Today, now, at once.

00:10:27.335 --> 00:10:33.028
The inspector quickly left the room.

00:10:33.088 --> 00:10:40.283
His name was Felix, and he was 33 years old.

00:10:40.343 --> 00:10:45.158
That was young for an inspector.

00:10:45.218 --> 00:10:48.918
But he was a good policeman.

00:10:48.978 --> 00:10:54.889
He liked his job and worked long hours.

00:10:54.949 --> 00:11:03.941
But he was sometimes afraid of Eva Heine, the chief of police.

00:11:04.001 --> 00:11:10.270
Ten minutes later, he was back in his office.

00:11:10.329 --> 00:11:15.028
and Adam came into his room.

00:11:15.088 --> 00:11:25.890
Adam was twenty-five and usually worked with Felix on important jobs.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.822
What did the chief say?

00:11:29.882 --> 00:11:32.372
Adam asked.

00:11:32.432 --> 00:11:35.663
Fine, Dean on, quickly.

00:11:35.723 --> 00:11:37.723
Felix said.

00:11:37.783 --> 00:11:41.221
So, let's begin.

00:11:41.281 --> 00:11:45.690
Have we got photographs of Dinon?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:50.302
And what about his family?

00:11:50.362 --> 00:11:56.504
Adam put some photographs on the desk.

00:11:56.564 --> 00:12:04.927
He's got a wife and two young children, he said.

00:12:04.987 --> 00:12:12.970
Right, I want photographs on television and in all the newspapers.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:26.883
Four men can watch his house and family day and night, four hours on and four hours off.

00:12:26.943 --> 00:13:13.309
Next, I want policemen at all the airports and telephones rang and people came and went in the office Felix and Adam worked on late into the night The second day.

00:13:13.369 --> 00:13:22.996
The next morning, Alex Denon was 40 kilometers south of the prison.

00:13:23.056 --> 00:13:30.310
He moved quickly and stayed away from towns and villages.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:40.908
It was winter and the weather was cold, so there were not many people in the fields.

00:13:40.968 --> 00:13:51.586
He looked behind him often, but nobody saw him and nobody followed him.

00:13:51.646 --> 00:14:02.172
At midday he found a quiet field and lay down under some small trees.

00:14:02.233 --> 00:14:06.922
He slept at once.

00:14:06.982 --> 00:14:20.285
At about three o'clock, Alex opened his eyes and saw an old woman in front of him.

00:14:20.345 --> 00:14:26.398
What are you doing in my field, young man?

00:14:26.458 --> 00:14:28.198
She said.

00:14:28.258 --> 00:14:31.952
Alex sat up quickly.

00:14:32.012 --> 00:14:35.496
I'm sorry," he said.

00:14:35.556 --> 00:14:40.696
I was tired and needed some sleep.

00:14:40.756 --> 00:14:43.437
I'm going now.

00:14:43.497 --> 00:14:49.498
You're very dirty, the old woman said.

00:14:49.558 --> 00:14:51.928
Look at you.

00:14:51.988 --> 00:14:55.279
Where are you going?

00:14:55.339 --> 00:14:59.330
North, Alex said.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.367
He stood up.

00:15:01.427 --> 00:15:05.325
and began to move away.

00:15:05.386 --> 00:15:08.227
Don't run away.

00:15:08.247 --> 00:15:13.219
I'm only an old woman.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:17.111
She looked at him carefully.

00:15:17.171 --> 00:15:23.474
You're dirty and hungry and tired and afraid.

00:15:23.494 --> 00:15:29.115
Am I right?

00:15:29.175 --> 00:15:34.626
Alex smiled slowly.

00:15:34.686 --> 00:15:38.018
Yes, he said.

00:15:38.078 --> 00:15:46.730
Well, come back to my house and have some food.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:53.424
And you can have some of my husband's old clothes.

00:15:53.484 --> 00:15:58.341
He died last winter.

00:15:58.401 --> 00:16:01.507
Alex looked at her.

00:16:01.568 --> 00:16:03.678
It was true.

00:16:03.738 --> 00:16:16.821
He was hungry and tired and dirty and afraid, but not of this old woman.

00:16:16.881 --> 00:16:22.256
Thank you very much, he said.

00:16:22.316 --> 00:16:27.103
The old woman's name was Marta.

00:16:27.163 --> 00:16:37.308
Her house was very small, but she put some wonderful hot food in front of Alex.

00:16:37.368 --> 00:16:42.962
He ate quickly, and Marta watched him.

00:16:43.022 --> 00:16:49.506
Oh, you were hungry, she laughed.

00:16:49.566 --> 00:16:56.363
Alex smiled but did not stop eating.

00:16:56.423 --> 00:17:04.720
Marta found some old clothes for him and then made some coffee.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:11.575
She said nothing but watched him with a smile.

00:17:11.635 --> 00:17:17.795
Alex finished eating and drank some coffee.

00:17:17.855 --> 00:17:22.443
He began to feel better.

00:17:22.502 --> 00:17:27.074
How did you escape from prison?

00:17:27.134 --> 00:17:30.205
Marta asked suddenly.

00:17:30.265 --> 00:17:33.636
Alex's face went white.

00:17:33.696 --> 00:17:39.068
He stared at Marta and said nothing.

00:17:39.128 --> 00:17:41.929
Marta laughed.

00:17:41.989 --> 00:17:45.838
It's all right, she said.

00:17:45.898 --> 00:17:51.012
I'm not afraid of the President's murderer.

00:17:51.072 --> 00:17:59.522
You can stay here tonight, Alex Denon, and have a good sleep.

00:17:59.582 --> 00:18:08.388
I don't like the police, and I'm not going to tell them.

00:18:08.448 --> 00:18:15.008
Felix and Adam did not get much sleep.

00:18:15.068 --> 00:18:22.460
They stayed in the office and slept between telephone calls.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.800
The phones rang often.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:32.972
But in the morning there was no news of Alex Deenon.

00:18:33.032 --> 00:18:36.471
The day went slowly.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:41.480
The phones rang again and again.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:45.312
But there was no news.

00:18:45.372 --> 00:18:48.104
Where is he?

00:18:48.164 --> 00:18:50.405
What's he doing?

00:18:50.465 --> 00:18:53.466
Felix said to Adam.

00:18:53.526 --> 00:18:55.608
He's hiding.

00:18:55.668 --> 00:18:59.019
Perhaps with friends.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:04.692
We questioned all his friends early this morning.

00:19:04.752 --> 00:19:07.034
Adam said.

00:19:07.094 --> 00:19:10.187
They said nothing.

00:19:10.247 --> 00:19:14.130
He looked at Felix.

00:19:14.191 --> 00:19:22.609
Can we bring some of them in here with their wives?

00:19:22.669 --> 00:19:29.740
Then we can ask more difficult questions.

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:34.158
Somebody usually talks then.

00:19:34.218 --> 00:19:38.520
No, Felix said coldly.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.912
That's not right.

00:19:40.971 --> 00:19:43.374
And you know it.

00:19:43.434 --> 00:19:47.716
Denon can't get out of the country now.

00:19:47.776 --> 00:19:51.698
But we need to find him today.

00:19:51.758 --> 00:19:57.532
The chief isn't going to be very happy.

00:19:57.592 --> 00:20:04.230
Late in the afternoon, the chief of police telephoned.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:11.954
Come to my office in half an hour, she told Felix.

00:20:12.014 --> 00:20:17.567
Felix felt tired and dirty.

00:20:17.628 --> 00:20:24.791
He quickly drank some black coffee and changed his shirt.

00:20:24.852 --> 00:20:33.137
Twenty minutes later, He stood in front of Eva Heine's desk.

00:20:33.197 --> 00:20:42.279
She did not smile, but looked at Felix and waited.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:51.011
The police are looking for Dinon in every town and village.

00:20:51.071 --> 00:20:53.922
Felix said quickly.

00:20:53.982 --> 00:21:03.640
We are watching the roads and the airports and the houses of his family and friends.

00:21:03.701 --> 00:21:10.544
Sit down, Inspector, and listen, the Chief said.

00:21:10.605 --> 00:21:14.707
We need to find this man quickly.

00:21:14.767 --> 00:21:18.690
The President is not happy.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:28.048
You're a good policeman, Inspector, and this is an important job for you.

00:21:28.108 --> 00:21:32.014
Chief, Felix began.

00:21:32.074 --> 00:21:36.216
How did Dinon escape from prison?

00:21:36.276 --> 00:21:41.588
That's not important now, the Chief said.

00:21:41.648 --> 00:21:47.492
But perhaps he had friends in prison, Felix said.

00:21:47.552 --> 00:21:50.633
Perhaps they know something.

00:21:50.693 --> 00:21:55.064
I need to talk to people at the prison.

00:21:55.124 --> 00:22:00.404
Well, you can't, the chief said.

00:22:00.464 --> 00:22:05.376
The telephone rang on the chief's desk.

00:22:05.436 --> 00:22:08.608
She picked up the phone.

00:22:08.668 --> 00:22:11.858
Evahine here.

00:22:11.918 --> 00:22:15.380
Then she smiled.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:20.411
Yes, Mr. President, she said.

00:22:20.471 --> 00:22:24.556
She listened for a minute or two.

00:22:24.616 --> 00:22:28.953
Yes, of course, Mr. President.

00:22:29.014 --> 00:22:31.666
I understand.

00:22:31.726 --> 00:22:33.727
Yes.

00:22:33.787 --> 00:22:35.838
Goodbye.

00:22:35.898 --> 00:22:43.204
Eva Heine put the phone down and looked at Felix Angrini.

00:22:43.264 --> 00:22:47.268
Forget Dinon's escape from prison.

00:22:47.327 --> 00:22:50.850
Get out there and find him.

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:55.945
And bring him back, dead or alive.

00:22:56.005 --> 00:23:02.860
At the door, Felix turned and looked at her.

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:08.162
Dead, he asked slowly.

00:23:08.222 --> 00:23:11.844
Dead men can't talk.

00:23:11.904 --> 00:23:14.034
Now go!

00:23:14.094 --> 00:23:19.227
Felix walked slowly back to his office.

00:23:19.287 --> 00:23:27.204
There were a lot of questions in his head, and he did not know the answers.

00:23:27.264 --> 00:23:32.159
Why can't I talk to people at the prison?"

00:23:32.219 --> 00:23:33.900
he thought.

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:39.862
What did the president say to the chief on the phone?

00:23:39.922 --> 00:23:44.495
And why does she want Dean on dead?

00:23:44.555 --> 00:23:50.398
He went to prison because he murdered the old president.

00:23:50.458 --> 00:23:53.410
Everybody knows that.

00:23:53.470 --> 00:24:08.061
What can he talk about now?

00:24:08.121 --> 00:24:22.512
The third day.

00:24:22.572 --> 00:24:33.417
Alex slept well for many hours, and the next morning, Marta put a big breakfast on the table.

00:24:33.477 --> 00:24:39.210
Alex ate hungrily, and Marta talked.

00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:43.192
What's happening to this country?

00:24:43.252 --> 00:24:47.137
She said, I don't know.

00:24:47.198 --> 00:24:51.033
I didn't like the old President.

00:24:51.093 --> 00:24:55.464
He was old and stupid.

00:24:55.524 --> 00:24:59.704
There's never much food in the shops.

00:24:59.764 --> 00:25:04.926
When did I last eat some good meat?

00:25:04.986 --> 00:25:07.666
She said angrily.

00:25:07.726 --> 00:25:11.267
I work every day.

00:25:11.327 --> 00:25:13.958
And what do I get?

00:25:14.018 --> 00:25:16.486
Nothing.

00:25:16.546 --> 00:25:21.175
What do you think about the new president then?"

00:25:21.236 --> 00:25:23.506
Alex asked.

00:25:23.567 --> 00:25:27.058
Oh, he's worse.

00:25:27.118 --> 00:25:36.234
He's a younger man, and he's not stupid, but he's more dangerous.

00:25:36.294 --> 00:25:47.740
He's very friendly with the police and the army, and he's putting a lot of people in prison.

00:25:47.800 --> 00:25:51.970
That's not good for the country.

00:25:52.030 --> 00:25:57.822
We want more food, not more prisoners."

00:25:57.882 --> 00:26:03.144
Just then, they heard somebody at the door.

00:26:03.204 --> 00:26:06.536
Quick, Marta said.

00:26:06.596 --> 00:26:11.848
Upstairs, hide under the bed.

00:26:11.908 --> 00:26:16.976
Alex ran upstairs and hid.

00:26:17.036 --> 00:26:23.728
Three minutes later, Marta came quickly upstairs.

00:26:23.788 --> 00:26:28.554
Her face was very angry.

00:26:28.614 --> 00:26:35.584
That was my friend George from the house down the road.

00:26:35.644 --> 00:26:41.010
Somebody saw you at the window this morning.

00:26:41.070 --> 00:26:46.014
It was that woman from the post office.

00:26:46.074 --> 00:26:54.440
The police give her money and she tells them all the secrets of the village.

00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:57.842
Everybody hates her.

00:26:57.902 --> 00:27:04.765
The police always have a friend in every village.

00:27:04.825 --> 00:27:07.486
Alex said sadly.

00:27:07.546 --> 00:27:12.889
Marta, I'm going now, at once.

00:27:12.949 --> 00:27:17.981
The police are going to be here soon, and ha!

00:27:18.042 --> 00:27:20.963
Marta said angrily.

00:27:21.024 --> 00:27:26.516
I'm not afraid of the police, or their questions.

00:27:26.576 --> 00:27:28.894
Alex Deanon?

00:27:28.954 --> 00:27:30.872
Who's he?

00:27:30.932 --> 00:27:35.314
Is he somebody on television?

00:27:35.374 --> 00:27:38.375
Alex smiled.

00:27:38.436 --> 00:27:43.398
You're a wonderful woman, Marta, he said.

00:27:43.458 --> 00:27:47.980
Goodbye and thank you.

00:27:48.040 --> 00:27:57.472
Marta looked at Alex and her old face was suddenly unhappy.

00:27:57.532 --> 00:28:02.894
Good luck, boy," she said.

00:28:02.954 --> 00:28:06.836
Alex left the house quickly.

00:28:06.896 --> 00:28:13.640
He went through Marta's back garden and out into the fields again.

00:28:13.700 --> 00:28:19.774
He felt better after the night in Marta's house.

00:28:19.834 --> 00:28:26.082
He thought about Marta and smiled.

00:28:26.142 --> 00:28:34.990
He was 33 years old and a dangerous murderer.

00:28:35.050 --> 00:28:43.714
But to Marta, he was only a tired and hungry boy.

00:28:43.774 --> 00:28:53.958
At 8 o'clock in the morning of the third day, the telephone rang on Felix's desk.

00:28:54.018 --> 00:28:59.713
Felix listened Then put the phone down quickly.

00:28:59.773 --> 00:29:03.166
Adam, he shouted.

00:29:03.226 --> 00:29:04.908
We've got him.

00:29:04.928 --> 00:29:08.610
He's in a village up north.

00:29:08.670 --> 00:29:11.464
In an old woman's house.

00:29:11.524 --> 00:29:13.054
Come on.

00:29:13.115 --> 00:29:15.327
Let's go.

00:29:15.387 --> 00:29:22.583
The big police car was fast and the kilometres went quickly.

00:29:22.643 --> 00:29:31.040
Adam was tired and wanted to sleep, but Felix wanted to talk.

00:29:31.100 --> 00:29:36.855
I saw the chief again last night, he said.

00:29:36.915 --> 00:29:39.768
She's getting angry.

00:29:39.828 --> 00:29:45.622
I was in her office, and the president phoned her.

00:29:45.682 --> 00:29:51.743
They want Dinon badly, dead or alive.

00:29:51.803 --> 00:29:55.712
Why do they want him dead?

00:29:55.772 --> 00:29:59.874
I don't know, Adam said.

00:29:59.934 --> 00:30:03.458
Let's find him first.

00:30:03.518 --> 00:30:10.634
In Marta's village, a policeman stood at the door of her house.

00:30:10.694 --> 00:30:18.690
We looked all through the house, and there's nobody in there, he said.

00:30:18.750 --> 00:30:26.021
Only Marta, the old woman, And she's not talking.

00:30:26.081 --> 00:30:33.317
Felix, Adam, and the policeman went into the house.

00:30:33.377 --> 00:30:37.490
Hello, Marta said.

00:30:37.550 --> 00:30:40.202
More policeman?

00:30:40.262 --> 00:30:43.796
What an exciting day.

00:30:43.856 --> 00:30:46.884
Listen to the inspector.

00:30:46.944 --> 00:30:49.592
Adam said angrily.

00:30:49.652 --> 00:30:54.505
He wants to ask you some questions.

00:30:54.565 --> 00:31:00.419
Felix sat down and smiled at Marta.

00:31:00.479 --> 00:31:11.196
Now, Marta, he said, somebody saw a young man in your house yesterday.

00:31:11.256 --> 00:31:14.148
Who was he, Marta?

00:31:14.208 --> 00:31:17.162
And where did he go?

00:31:17.222 --> 00:31:21.775
He was my sister's youngest son.

00:31:21.835 --> 00:31:24.326
Marta said happily.

00:31:24.386 --> 00:31:28.548
He's a very nice boy.

00:31:28.608 --> 00:31:33.819
The policeman whispered in Felix's ear.

00:31:33.879 --> 00:31:38.890
Felix looked sadly at Marta.

00:31:38.950 --> 00:31:48.026
Your sister and all her family live in Australia, Marta.

00:31:48.086 --> 00:31:52.370
Who was the man in your house?

00:31:52.430 --> 00:31:56.772
Oh dear, Marta said.

00:31:56.832 --> 00:32:00.042
I'm an old woman, you know.

00:32:00.102 --> 00:32:03.164
Seventy-two last month.

00:32:03.224 --> 00:32:06.735
I forget things very easily.

00:32:06.755 --> 00:32:12.162
In Australia, did you say?

00:32:12.222 --> 00:32:21.412
Felix asked question after question, but Marta told him nothing.

00:32:21.471 --> 00:32:28.746
Sometimes, the young man in her house was her sister's son.

00:32:28.807 --> 00:32:35.362
Sometimes, he was the young doctor from the next village.

00:32:35.422 --> 00:32:42.367
But he was never Alex Dinon, the president's murderer.

00:32:42.427 --> 00:32:48.582
Adam got very angry and whispered to Felix.

00:32:48.642 --> 00:32:52.224
Can I ask the questions?

00:32:52.284 --> 00:32:55.716
No, Felix said.

00:32:55.777 --> 00:32:59.828
He did not like Adam's questions.

00:32:59.888 --> 00:33:04.552
He stood up and moved to the door.

00:33:04.612 --> 00:33:10.557
But Marta now wanted to ask him a question.

00:33:10.617 --> 00:33:15.773
And why do you work for the police, young man?

00:33:15.793 --> 00:33:23.752
The police always put the wrong people in prison, you know?

00:33:23.812 --> 00:33:28.737
Marta, Felix said tiredly.

00:33:28.797 --> 00:33:32.981
Alex Deenon is a murderer.

00:33:33.040 --> 00:33:39.064
He murdered, oh, I know that," Marta said.

00:33:39.125 --> 00:33:42.938
The newspapers said that.

00:33:42.998 --> 00:33:50.744
But newspapers and the television never tell us the true story.

00:33:50.764 --> 00:33:55.913
Alex D'Non isn't a murderer.

00:33:55.973 --> 00:33:58.859
He's a nice young man.

00:33:58.879 --> 00:34:05.202
A nice young man, Felix said quickly.

00:34:05.262 --> 00:34:08.113
How do you know that?

00:34:08.173 --> 00:34:11.104
He's got a nice face.

00:34:11.164 --> 00:34:16.947
That's why I saw his picture on the television.

00:34:16.967 --> 00:34:25.510
I'm an old woman and I can read people's faces.

00:34:25.571 --> 00:34:30.273
So who did murder the president then?

00:34:30.334 --> 00:34:32.815
Felix asked.

00:34:32.875 --> 00:34:37.498
I don't know, Marta said.

00:34:37.558 --> 00:34:39.699
You're the policeman.

00:34:39.719 --> 00:34:44.153
You go and find the murderer.

00:34:44.212 --> 00:34:47.184
But I can tell you one thing.

00:34:47.204 --> 00:34:53.161
You can begin with the new president.

00:34:53.222 --> 00:34:57.498
He's got a murderer's face.

00:34:57.558 --> 00:35:02.780
Adam said angrily, that's dangerous talk.

00:35:02.841 --> 00:35:08.163
Marta laughed, and Felix opened the door.

00:35:08.224 --> 00:35:13.766
Let's go, Adam, he said quietly.

00:35:13.826 --> 00:35:20.530
Out in the road, Adam said, stupid old woman.

00:35:20.591 --> 00:35:27.321
Yes, Felix said, Perhaps she was.

00:35:27.381 --> 00:35:32.064
And perhaps she wasn't.

00:35:32.124 --> 00:35:46.114
The fourth day.

00:35:46.174 --> 00:36:03.558
After he left Marta's village, Alex moved quickly and quietly across the fields.

00:36:03.618 --> 00:36:05.870
Nobody saw him.

00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:10.692
He walked and ran and walked again.

00:36:10.752 --> 00:36:15.629
It rained all day and all night.

00:36:15.689 --> 00:36:27.256
He walked through the night, and the next morning, the fourth day, he was very tired and very hungry.

00:36:27.316 --> 00:36:40.020
He hid in some trees for an hour or two, and then he went on south, always south to his hometown.

00:36:40.080 --> 00:36:44.521
Where can I go, he thought?

00:36:44.581 --> 00:36:48.452
Perhaps I can escape from the country.

00:36:48.512 --> 00:36:54.106
But I want to see Olivia again before I leave.

00:36:54.166 --> 00:36:58.668
Or before the police find me.

00:36:58.728 --> 00:37:02.832
But first, he needed food.

00:37:02.892 --> 00:37:06.394
He had some money in his pocket.

00:37:06.454 --> 00:37:08.656
Marta's money.

00:37:08.716 --> 00:37:11.783
He remembered her words.

00:37:11.843 --> 00:37:14.350
You take it.

00:37:14.410 --> 00:37:17.092
I don't need it.

00:37:17.152 --> 00:37:22.434
An old woman doesn't need money.

00:37:22.495 --> 00:37:25.206
Alex smiled.

00:37:25.266 --> 00:37:29.989
What a wonderful old woman.

00:37:30.049 --> 00:37:40.759
He came to a small town on a river and found a food shop in a quiet street.

00:37:40.819 --> 00:37:45.724
He opened the door and went in.

00:37:45.784 --> 00:37:53.307
There were a lot of people in the shop and he waited quietly behind them.

00:37:53.367 --> 00:37:56.209
People looked at him.

00:37:56.269 --> 00:37:59.960
and a man went out quickly.

00:38:00.020 --> 00:38:08.192
Alex wanted to run, but he was very hungry, so he waited.

00:38:08.252 --> 00:38:14.224
Then a woman with her young son came into the shop.

00:38:14.284 --> 00:38:22.769
The woman whispered to the boy, and the boy came up to Alex.

00:38:22.829 --> 00:38:30.314
There are two policemen in the street, he said very quietly.

00:38:30.374 --> 00:38:33.575
And they're coming here.

00:38:33.635 --> 00:38:37.896
Alex looked quickly at the door.

00:38:37.956 --> 00:38:41.367
But he could not escape now.

00:38:41.427 --> 00:38:44.637
Then the shopkeeper called to him.

00:38:44.657 --> 00:38:47.578
Hey you!

00:38:47.638 --> 00:38:49.958
He said, quick!

00:38:50.018 --> 00:38:52.818
Go out through the back!

00:38:52.878 --> 00:39:00.201
Alex ran through the back of the shop and the shopkeeper followed him.

00:39:00.261 --> 00:39:03.583
I never helped the police.

00:39:03.644 --> 00:39:07.056
They're all bad, he said.

00:39:07.116 --> 00:39:11.819
He opened the back door and looked out.

00:39:11.879 --> 00:39:16.432
It's okay, he said quickly.

00:39:16.493 --> 00:39:21.545
You can get out of town along the river.

00:39:21.605 --> 00:39:25.026
follow the back of the houses.

00:39:25.087 --> 00:39:27.757
Nobody goes there.

00:39:27.818 --> 00:39:29.908
Good luck.

00:39:29.968 --> 00:39:31.710
Thank you.

00:39:31.770 --> 00:39:35.702
Alex said and ran.

00:39:35.762 --> 00:39:42.564
Three kilometres from the town, Alex came to a road.

00:39:42.625 --> 00:39:45.776
He crossed the road quickly.

00:39:45.836 --> 00:39:50.688
But a lorry came along at the same time.

00:39:50.748 --> 00:39:54.440
The lorry slowed down.

00:39:54.500 --> 00:39:58.653
And the driver called out to him.

00:39:58.713 --> 00:40:01.794
Where are you going?

00:40:01.855 --> 00:40:05.978
Alex said the name of his hometown.

00:40:06.038 --> 00:40:09.970
And the driver said, Come on.

00:40:10.030 --> 00:40:12.632
I'm going near there.

00:40:12.692 --> 00:40:15.504
You can come with me.

00:40:15.564 --> 00:40:25.490
Alex got into the front of the lorry, and the driver looked carefully into his face.

00:40:25.550 --> 00:40:27.931
Do I know you?

00:40:27.951 --> 00:40:30.572
He asked.

00:40:30.632 --> 00:40:35.976
Alex said nothing, and waited.

00:40:36.036 --> 00:40:39.837
He felt very tired.

00:40:39.898 --> 00:40:43.960
The driver stared at him for a minute.

00:40:44.020 --> 00:40:46.467
Then he smiled.

00:40:46.527 --> 00:40:47.693
No.

00:40:47.713 --> 00:40:52.364
I don't know you, he said.

00:40:52.424 --> 00:40:55.646
Get into the back of the lorry.

00:40:55.706 --> 00:40:59.437
Nobody can see you there.

00:40:59.497 --> 00:41:02.288
Are you hungry?

00:41:02.348 --> 00:41:05.979
Yes, I am, Alex said.

00:41:06.039 --> 00:41:07.570
Very.

00:41:07.630 --> 00:41:11.881
Well, I've got some sandwiches.

00:41:11.941 --> 00:41:13.942
Here you are.

00:41:14.002 --> 00:41:15.416
No.

00:41:15.476 --> 00:41:22.332
Get in the back quickly before we see a police car.

00:41:22.392 --> 00:41:26.926
The lorry drove slowly south.

00:41:26.986 --> 00:41:36.912
Alex ate all the driver's sandwiches and then slept like a dead man.

00:41:36.972 --> 00:41:46.886
We are always three hours or more behind him, Felix said to Adam in the car.

00:41:46.946 --> 00:41:57.668
We drive up and down the country, but Denon always moves on before we get there.

00:41:57.728 --> 00:42:05.252
Perhaps this shopkeeper can tell us something, Adam said.

00:42:05.312 --> 00:42:10.128
But the shopkeeper was not helpful.

00:42:10.188 --> 00:42:12.328
Alex who?

00:42:12.388 --> 00:42:14.050
He said.

00:42:14.110 --> 00:42:18.592
Dean on Felix shouted.

00:42:18.652 --> 00:42:21.374
He was very tired.

00:42:21.435 --> 00:42:26.007
He escaped from prison five days ago.

00:42:26.067 --> 00:42:30.730
Somebody saw him in your shop.

00:42:30.790 --> 00:42:34.945
I don't have prisoners in my shop.

00:42:35.005 --> 00:42:38.380
The shopkeeper said angrily.

00:42:38.440 --> 00:42:42.982
And I don't want the police here.

00:42:43.042 --> 00:42:47.473
Did Deenon come into this shop?

00:42:47.533 --> 00:42:50.094
Felix asked.

00:42:50.154 --> 00:42:52.515
Deenon!

00:42:52.575 --> 00:42:56.316
The shopkeeper said slowly.

00:42:56.377 --> 00:42:59.778
What did he do?

00:42:59.839 --> 00:43:02.370
Wait a minute!

00:43:02.430 --> 00:43:04.375
Yes!

00:43:04.436 --> 00:43:11.036
Did he write a book about the old president?

00:43:11.096 --> 00:43:15.688
He killed the president, Adam said.

00:43:15.748 --> 00:43:17.490
He murdered him.

00:43:17.510 --> 00:43:23.674
Oh yes, the shopkeeper said.

00:43:23.734 --> 00:43:26.526
I remember now.

00:43:26.587 --> 00:43:30.150
It was a good book.

00:43:30.210 --> 00:43:40.252
But the president's murderer Did not come into my shop this morning.

00:43:40.312 --> 00:43:46.207
Felix watched the shopkeeper's face carefully.

00:43:46.267 --> 00:43:54.664
My question, he said, asked about Alex Dynon.

00:43:54.724 --> 00:44:02.676
The shopkeeper looked at Felix and smiled slowly.

00:44:02.736 --> 00:44:07.576
That's right," he said.

00:44:07.636 --> 00:44:21.176
Felix and Adam talked to a lot of people and asked a lot of questions in that small town, but they learned nothing.

00:44:21.236 --> 00:44:29.284
Later, back in the office, Felix was very quiet.

00:44:29.344 --> 00:44:41.250
Suddenly, he looked at Adam across the desk and said, We can't get Deenon's book in this country.

00:44:41.310 --> 00:44:44.862
Do you know it, Adam?

00:44:44.922 --> 00:44:48.835
No, Adam said.

00:44:48.896 --> 00:44:54.051
Felix stared at the telephone on his desk.

00:44:54.111 --> 00:44:57.466
Where is Denon?

00:44:57.526 --> 00:45:00.066
He said slowly.

00:45:00.126 --> 00:45:02.988
People are helping him.

00:45:03.048 --> 00:45:04.269
But why?

00:45:04.289 --> 00:45:07.260
He's a murderer.

00:45:07.321 --> 00:45:11.563
And nobody wants to help us.

00:45:11.623 --> 00:45:17.246
People never help the police in this country.

00:45:17.306 --> 00:45:19.467
Adam said.

00:45:19.528 --> 00:45:23.439
People don't like us.

00:45:23.499 --> 00:45:27.832
Why are we policemen, Adam?

00:45:27.892 --> 00:45:31.725
It's a good job, Adam said.

00:45:31.745 --> 00:45:35.998
Earn the money's good.

00:45:36.058 --> 00:45:45.296
After a minute or two, Felix said, did Dean on murder the president?

00:45:45.356 --> 00:45:48.278
What do you think, Adam?

00:45:48.339 --> 00:45:54.234
Well, why did they put him in prison then?

00:45:54.294 --> 00:46:00.508
That doesn't answer my question, Felix said.

00:46:00.568 --> 00:46:05.870
I do my job, Adam said.

00:46:05.930 --> 00:46:10.782
And I don't ask questions.

00:46:10.842 --> 00:46:26.102
Felix looked at him, but said nothing.

00:46:26.162 --> 00:46:46.586
The fifth day in an old house in a quiet road, a woman waited.

00:46:46.646 --> 00:46:54.030
She waited day and night and did not sleep.

00:46:54.090 --> 00:47:04.166
At nine o'clock in the evening of the fifth day, she heard a noise at the window at the back of the house.

00:47:04.226 --> 00:47:09.858
Quickly she ran and opened the window.

00:47:09.918 --> 00:47:16.240
A minute later she was in Alex's arms.

00:47:16.301 --> 00:47:22.144
They did not speak for a long time.

00:47:22.204 --> 00:47:31.670
Then they talked quietly about their friends and their family.

00:47:31.730 --> 00:47:38.846
The children are with my sister, Olivia said.

00:47:38.906 --> 00:47:42.448
It's better for them there.

00:47:42.508 --> 00:47:47.880
But I came here to Rudy's house.

00:47:47.940 --> 00:47:50.411
Rudy's away.

00:47:50.472 --> 00:47:56.594
And poorly told me this was the best place to wait.

00:47:56.654 --> 00:48:03.746
I wanted to see you before you leave the country.

00:48:03.806 --> 00:48:10.018
Oh, Alex, I'm so afraid for you?

00:48:10.078 --> 00:48:12.190
Yes.

00:48:12.250 --> 00:48:18.072
Escape is going to be difficult, Alex said.

00:48:18.132 --> 00:48:22.404
I talked to Paulie on the phone.

00:48:22.464 --> 00:48:24.366
The police?

00:48:24.426 --> 00:48:31.988
Yes, but you escaped from prison, Olivia said quickly.

00:48:32.048 --> 00:48:35.380
You have a lot of friends.

00:48:35.440 --> 00:48:38.982
Perhaps Polly can help you.

00:48:39.042 --> 00:48:44.656
Or perhaps I've got some good friends.

00:48:44.716 --> 00:48:47.086
I know that.

00:48:47.147 --> 00:48:52.060
But I've got a lot of enemies too.

00:48:52.120 --> 00:48:55.132
Alex said slowly.

00:48:55.192 --> 00:48:59.696
Very dangerous enemies.

00:48:59.756 --> 00:49:04.920
Suddenly, Olivia saw his hands.

00:49:04.980 --> 00:49:07.210
Your hands?

00:49:07.270 --> 00:49:09.400
Oh, Alex.

00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:13.472
What happened to your hands?

00:49:13.532 --> 00:49:17.593
Alex looked down at them.

00:49:17.653 --> 00:49:21.604
It happened in prison.

00:49:21.665 --> 00:49:24.195
He said slowly.

00:49:24.255 --> 00:49:27.976
They did it with a knife.

00:49:28.036 --> 00:49:31.376
and cigarettes.

00:49:31.437 --> 00:49:39.818
But why, Olivia whispered, why did they do that?

00:49:39.878 --> 00:49:46.479
They wanted a name, but I didn't tell them.

00:49:46.539 --> 00:49:49.010
What name?

00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:54.550
The name of the President's murderer.

00:49:54.610 --> 00:49:57.946
But they say you killed him.

00:49:58.006 --> 00:49:59.952
Olivia began.

00:50:00.012 --> 00:50:05.518
Yes, but I did not kill the president.

00:50:05.578 --> 00:50:09.722
And the police know that.

00:50:09.782 --> 00:50:15.888
So they put you in prison, Olivia said.

00:50:15.948 --> 00:50:19.992
Because they needed a murderer.

00:50:20.053 --> 00:50:21.855
Yes.

00:50:21.915 --> 00:50:34.736
And because of my book about the old president and the government of this country, it was a very angry book.

00:50:34.796 --> 00:50:37.358
Do you remember?

00:50:37.418 --> 00:50:40.310
Alex smiled.

00:50:40.370 --> 00:50:46.507
But the old president read it and liked it.

00:50:46.568 --> 00:50:54.138
He wasn't a bad man, and he wanted a better life for the people.

00:50:54.198 --> 00:51:01.128
He wanted to change things in this country, but he couldn't.

00:51:01.188 --> 00:51:06.490
The police and the army stopped him.

00:51:06.550 --> 00:51:15.236
And the new president, of course, is a good friend of the police and the army.

00:51:15.296 --> 00:51:18.369
A very good friend.

00:51:18.429 --> 00:51:21.292
Alex laughed angrily.

00:51:21.352 --> 00:51:23.794
You see, Olivia.

00:51:23.854 --> 00:51:30.718
The police know the murderer's name, but it's a secret.

00:51:30.778 --> 00:51:36.101
They don't want people in this country to know the name.

00:51:36.162 --> 00:51:45.296
And so they were angry with me in prison because they think that I know the murderer's name.

00:51:45.356 --> 00:51:50.806
Olivia's face was afraid.

00:51:50.866 --> 00:51:54.215
Do you know?"

00:51:54.275 --> 00:51:56.336
she whispered.

00:51:56.396 --> 00:52:04.142
Yes, Alex looked at his wife's white unhappy face.

00:52:04.202 --> 00:52:10.906
But I'm not going to tell you, he said quietly.

00:52:10.966 --> 00:52:16.602
It's a very dangerous name.

00:52:16.662 --> 00:52:23.340
Alex ate some food and changed his clothes.

00:52:23.400 --> 00:52:32.597
Then he slept and Olivia watched the road through the windows.

00:52:32.657 --> 00:52:39.023
In his office Felix waited for more news.

00:52:39.083 --> 00:52:42.716
He waited and he thought.

00:52:42.776 --> 00:53:03.118
about his job, about the dead president, and the new president, about the old woman, Marta, about Eva Heine, the chief of police, and about Alex Denon.

00:53:03.178 --> 00:53:10.252
At 9.05 PM, the telephone rang on Felix's desk.

00:53:10.312 --> 00:53:17.414
He listened, Then quickly jumped to his feet, and called to Adam.

00:53:17.475 --> 00:53:22.478
Dean ons in his hometown, he shouted.

00:53:22.538 --> 00:53:26.230
He's in his old teacher's house.

00:53:26.290 --> 00:53:30.482
He went in three minutes ago.

00:53:30.542 --> 00:53:32.984
Adam laughed.

00:53:33.044 --> 00:53:38.066
We've got him now, he said happily.

00:53:38.126 --> 00:53:42.186
Listen, Felix said quickly.

00:53:42.246 --> 00:53:50.351
Take ten more men with you, and drive down to Denon's town at once.

00:53:50.412 --> 00:53:56.797
Wait near the house and watch, but don't go in.

00:53:56.857 --> 00:54:02.852
I'm going to phone the chief now, and then follow you.

00:54:02.912 --> 00:54:09.110
Right, Adam said, and quickly left the room.

00:54:09.170 --> 00:54:15.646
Felix phoned the chief and told her the news.

00:54:15.706 --> 00:54:20.297
Good, the chief said.

00:54:20.358 --> 00:54:23.018
Now wait there.

00:54:23.078 --> 00:54:29.041
I want to speak to you again in 10 minutes.

00:54:29.101 --> 00:54:32.412
Felix waited angrily.

00:54:32.473 --> 00:54:35.884
He wanted to leave at once.

00:54:35.944 --> 00:54:38.333
He wanted to talk.

00:54:38.393 --> 00:54:40.782
to Alex Deenon.

00:54:40.842 --> 00:54:46.896
Perhaps Deenon knew the answers to Felix's questions.

00:54:46.956 --> 00:54:53.490
The phone rang and Felix picked it up quickly.

00:54:53.550 --> 00:54:56.872
Now listen, Inspector.

00:54:56.932 --> 00:55:00.063
Don't go into the house.

00:55:00.124 --> 00:55:04.589
Wait in the road and watch.

00:55:04.649 --> 00:55:11.777
But we can go into the house and get him," Felix said.

00:55:11.837 --> 00:55:13.808
Why not?

00:55:13.868 --> 00:55:17.892
No, that's dangerous.

00:55:17.952 --> 00:55:23.456
Perhaps his wife and children are in the house.

00:55:23.516 --> 00:55:28.480
But his children are with his wife's sister.

00:55:28.540 --> 00:55:30.430
We know that.

00:55:30.490 --> 00:55:32.289
Felix said.

00:55:32.349 --> 00:55:37.142
So, listen to me, Inspector.

00:55:37.203 --> 00:55:41.636
Felix did not answer.

00:55:41.696 --> 00:55:47.570
Are you listening to me, Inspector?

00:55:47.630 --> 00:55:50.302
Yes, Chief.

00:55:50.362 --> 00:55:53.254
Felix said quietly.

00:55:53.314 --> 00:55:58.586
Now, Dinon can't stay in the house.

00:55:58.646 --> 00:56:07.200
He's going to come out later in the night when the streets are quiet.

00:56:07.261 --> 00:56:10.132
He can't escape.

00:56:10.192 --> 00:56:13.074
The soldiers, soldiers?

00:56:13.134 --> 00:56:14.595
What soldiers?

00:56:14.655 --> 00:56:16.796
Felix said angrily.

00:56:16.857 --> 00:56:19.168
I don't need the army.

00:56:19.188 --> 00:56:27.116
This man, Denon, is very, very important in Spectre.

00:56:27.176 --> 00:56:30.350
You need help.

00:56:30.410 --> 00:56:35.494
And the army is going to help you.

00:56:35.554 --> 00:56:42.389
They're putting 300 men in all the roads near the house.

00:56:42.449 --> 00:56:48.393
I want Dinon tonight, Inspector.

00:56:48.454 --> 00:56:58.132
The Chief put the phone down and Felix stared at his desk.

00:56:58.192 --> 00:57:04.378
alive or dead he thought.

00:57:04.438 --> 00:57:12.752
Which does she and our new President want?

00:57:12.812 --> 00:57:17.853
I think I know the answer.

00:57:17.914 --> 00:57:25.720
They want him dead and I want to know why.

00:57:25.780 --> 00:57:35.106
The police car took Felix to Denon's hometown an hour away.

00:57:35.167 --> 00:57:42.170
And Felix found Adam in a quiet street behind the house.

00:57:42.230 --> 00:57:48.192
They sat in Adam's car and talked.

00:57:48.252 --> 00:57:52.813
Adam looked at Felix's face.

00:57:52.874 --> 00:57:55.904
What are you angry about?

00:57:55.964 --> 00:57:57.618
He asked.

00:57:57.678 --> 00:58:01.242
D-Nons in the house!

00:58:01.303 --> 00:58:05.003
And he can't escape now!

00:58:05.063 --> 00:58:08.904
When he comes out, wham!

00:58:08.964 --> 00:58:11.704
We've got him!

00:58:11.764 --> 00:58:22.636
I'm angry, Felix said, because half the army with its guns is in this town tonight.

00:58:22.696 --> 00:58:26.254
I wanted to go into the house.

00:58:26.314 --> 00:58:36.212
But I can't because the chief said no and the soldiers are watching the house.

00:58:36.272 --> 00:58:42.054
But I wanted to get to dean on first.

00:58:42.114 --> 00:58:47.486
That's going to be difficult, Adam said.

00:58:47.546 --> 00:58:55.088
Soldiers shoot first and ask questions later.

00:58:55.148 --> 00:59:00.556
Yes, Felix said slowly.

00:59:00.616 --> 00:59:19.381
They're going to kill Alex Denon, and I can't stop them.

00:59:19.441 --> 00:59:32.612
The sixth day.

00:59:32.672 --> 00:59:42.596
At three o'clock in the morning, Alex got up from the bed and looked out of the window.

00:59:42.656 --> 00:59:46.738
Olivia opened her eyes.

00:59:46.798 --> 00:59:49.328
Are you?

00:59:49.388 --> 00:59:52.200
Are you leaving now?

00:59:52.260 --> 00:59:54.070
She asked.

00:59:54.130 --> 00:59:58.174
Yes, Alex said.

00:59:58.234 --> 01:00:01.569
I can't stay longer.

01:00:01.629 --> 01:00:06.162
Perhaps the police are out there now.

01:00:06.222 --> 01:00:10.286
They're watching all our friends' houses.

01:00:10.346 --> 01:00:13.077
Paulie told me.

01:00:13.137 --> 01:00:17.100
He put on his shoes and coat.

01:00:17.160 --> 01:00:21.143
Then looked at his wife.

01:00:21.203 --> 01:00:24.775
Olivia, listen.

01:00:24.835 --> 01:00:31.400
be very careful and live very quietly.

01:00:31.460 --> 01:00:47.614
The police are going to watch you for some time, wait for a year, then take the children and leave the country secretly.

01:00:47.674 --> 01:00:51.412
Our friends can help you.

01:00:51.472 --> 01:01:01.080
Find a new home in a new country and make a new life.

01:01:01.140 --> 01:01:04.812
Olivia began to cry.

01:01:04.872 --> 01:01:11.544
But Alex, you're going to be there with us.

01:01:11.604 --> 01:01:14.996
Alex smiled.

01:01:15.056 --> 01:01:19.444
Yes, perhaps.

01:01:19.504 --> 01:01:28.003
He took his wife's face in his hands and looked into her unhappy eyes.

01:01:28.063 --> 01:01:31.394
Don't cry, my love.

01:01:31.454 --> 01:01:34.415
He said quietly.

01:01:34.475 --> 01:01:39.146
Give me a smile before I go.

01:01:39.166 --> 01:01:45.928
Oh, Alex, I'm afraid.

01:01:45.988 --> 01:01:49.966
Olivia could not stop crying.

01:01:50.026 --> 01:01:51.523
I love you.

01:01:51.543 --> 01:01:53.904
I love you."

01:01:53.964 --> 01:01:55.726
She whispered.

01:01:55.786 --> 01:02:02.650
Go quickly and be careful, please.

01:02:02.710 --> 01:02:07.494
Alex smiled sadly.

01:02:07.554 --> 01:02:12.168
Goodbye, my love.

01:02:12.228 --> 01:02:19.228
He left the house quickly and went out into the dark night.

01:02:19.288 --> 01:02:25.468
He waited for ten minutes at the door and listened.

01:02:25.528 --> 01:02:31.262
But he heard nothing and saw nothing.

01:02:31.322 --> 01:02:36.616
He came out into the road very carefully.

01:02:36.676 --> 01:02:40.238
Again he waited.

01:02:40.298 --> 01:02:48.962
From an upstairs window in his house, a white face watched him.

01:02:49.022 --> 01:02:55.054
Then Alex began to walk quickly along the road.

01:02:55.114 --> 01:03:02.549
He stayed near the houses and looked behind him again and again.

01:03:02.609 --> 01:03:08.664
Two hundred meters along the road there was a car.

01:03:08.724 --> 01:03:18.854
Alex stared at it but there was nobody in the car and he walked quickly past.

01:03:18.914 --> 01:03:26.483
Suddenly, there were noises and lights and soldiers with guns.

01:03:26.543 --> 01:03:33.088
Alex began to run, but he did not run far.

01:03:33.148 --> 01:03:35.319
There was a shot.

01:03:35.380 --> 01:03:41.334
Two, three, four, five shots.

01:03:41.394 --> 01:03:47.879
And Alex did not move again.

01:03:47.939 --> 01:03:54.612
Felix ran across the road and looked at the body.

01:03:54.672 --> 01:03:58.412
Adam was there before him.

01:03:58.472 --> 01:04:01.023
Is he alive?

01:04:01.083 --> 01:04:04.124
Felix asked quickly.

01:04:04.184 --> 01:04:07.634
No, he's dead.

01:04:07.694 --> 01:04:12.636
Adams stood up and looked at Felix.

01:04:12.696 --> 01:04:18.042
Very, very dead, he said.

01:04:18.102 --> 01:04:21.768
Felix's face was angry.

01:04:21.828 --> 01:04:26.782
The soldiers killed him, he said.

01:04:26.842 --> 01:04:30.654
Adam looked at Felix.

01:04:30.714 --> 01:04:34.496
Well, that's their job.

01:04:34.556 --> 01:04:40.378
Dean on ran away, so the soldiers shot him.

01:04:40.438 --> 01:04:44.728
Alive or dead, the chief said.

01:04:44.788 --> 01:04:47.508
But we found him.

01:04:47.568 --> 01:04:50.860
That's the important thing.

01:04:50.920 --> 01:04:56.775
Felix stared down at Alex Dinaan's face.

01:04:56.835 --> 01:05:00.438
I wanted to talk to him.

01:05:00.498 --> 01:05:01.919
To ask him.

01:05:01.939 --> 01:05:05.732
To ask him what?

01:05:05.792 --> 01:05:07.824
Adam said.

01:05:07.884 --> 01:05:11.380
Felix did not answer.

01:05:11.440 --> 01:05:16.506
He looked down at the dead body on the road.

01:05:16.566 --> 01:05:19.628
Then he turned away.

01:05:19.688 --> 01:05:23.290
Nothing, he said.

01:05:23.350 --> 01:05:26.198
It doesn't matter.

01:05:26.258 --> 01:05:30.759
There was a lot of noise in the road now.

01:05:30.819 --> 01:05:35.212
Soldiers and policemen moved here and there.

01:05:35.272 --> 01:05:38.776
Police cars came and went.

01:05:38.836 --> 01:05:48.124
The people in the houses looked out of their windows, but they did not open their doors.

01:05:48.184 --> 01:05:53.874
It was better not to ask questions.

01:05:53.935 --> 01:06:01.166
An ambulance came and took the body away.

01:06:01.226 --> 01:06:08.800
Later that day, Felix went back to the chief's office.

01:06:08.860 --> 01:06:13.394
The chief called him into her room.

01:06:13.454 --> 01:06:17.686
So he's dead, she said.

01:06:17.746 --> 01:06:20.358
Well done, Felix.

01:06:20.418 --> 01:06:25.346
The president is very pleased with you.

01:06:25.406 --> 01:06:31.123
The chief did not often say, Felix.

01:06:31.184 --> 01:06:36.906
Usually, she called him Inspector.

01:06:36.966 --> 01:06:43.748
Felix sat down and looked at either hind.

01:06:43.808 --> 01:06:48.730
A lot of people think he stopped.

01:06:48.790 --> 01:06:52.092
Then he began again.

01:06:52.152 --> 01:07:01.546
They say, Alex Deenon wasn't the president's murderer.

01:07:01.606 --> 01:07:07.280
People say a lot of things, the chief said.

01:07:07.340 --> 01:07:09.580
She smiled.

01:07:09.640 --> 01:07:13.022
But they're not all true.

01:07:13.082 --> 01:07:16.855
Don't listen to stories, Felix.

01:07:16.916 --> 01:07:19.797
You've got a good job.

01:07:19.857 --> 01:07:23.898
Don't ask questions.

01:07:23.958 --> 01:07:32.531
But perhaps, Felix said slowly, the stories are true.

01:07:32.591 --> 01:07:38.263
And it's a policeman's job to ask questions.

01:07:38.323 --> 01:07:44.355
Eva Heinz stood up and came nearer to Felix.

01:07:44.416 --> 01:07:52.246
She looked down into his face and her gray eyes were cold.

01:07:52.306 --> 01:07:55.726
Listen," she said.

01:07:55.786 --> 01:08:00.740
Somebody murdered the old president, right?

01:08:00.801 --> 01:08:05.404
And our new president needed a murderer.

01:08:05.464 --> 01:08:06.906
Quickly.

01:08:06.966 --> 01:08:13.411
So we found a murderer for him, Alex Dinaum.

01:08:13.471 --> 01:08:18.176
We don't kill murderers in this country.

01:08:18.236 --> 01:08:20.951
They go to prison.

01:08:21.011 --> 01:08:28.137
but Dinon escaped from prison, and now he's dead.

01:08:28.197 --> 01:08:35.730
The murderer is dead Felix, and that's the end of the story.

01:08:35.790 --> 01:08:40.011
It was very quiet in the room.

01:08:40.070 --> 01:08:45.571
The chief watched Felix and waited.

01:08:45.631 --> 01:08:53.004
Felix looked down at his hands and said nothing.

01:08:53.064 --> 01:09:01.009
Then he looked up into either hinds cold eyes.

01:09:01.069 --> 01:09:04.502
Who murdered the President?

01:09:04.562 --> 01:09:06.565
He asked.

01:09:06.624 --> 01:09:11.379
Eva Hein's face did not change.

01:09:11.439 --> 01:09:19.473
She stared at Felix and Felix stared back at her.

01:09:19.533 --> 01:09:30.218
After a long time, Eva Hein said, perhaps you need a new job, Felix.

01:09:30.278 --> 01:09:35.722
Think about it very carefully.

01:09:35.783 --> 01:09:39.998
The young man looked at her face.

01:09:40.058 --> 01:09:45.372
Then he looked away out of the window.

01:09:45.432 --> 01:09:52.549
After a minute or two he stood up and went to the door.

01:09:52.609 --> 01:10:00.140
Then he turned and looked at the chief of police.

01:10:00.200 --> 01:10:08.829
I'd like to know the murderer's name," he said quietly.

01:10:08.889 --> 01:10:12.720
And I'm going to find it.

01:10:12.780 --> 01:10:15.992
He opened the door.

01:10:16.052 --> 01:10:19.384
Goodbye, Chief.

01:10:19.444 --> 01:10:27.927
He went out and closed the door behind him for the last time.

